==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sh|sla-pro|*leděnъ}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ru|-}} {{m|ru|ледяной}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/lêden/|lang=sh}}
* {{hyphenation|led|en|lang=sh}}

===Adjective===
{{sh-adj|head=lȅden|def=ledeni|def_a=lȅdenī|comp=ledeniji|comp_a=ledènijī|r|леден|ле̏ден}}

# [[icy]], [[glacial]] (made of ice)
# full of ice
# [[cold]], [[frigid]], [[chilled]]
# [[crystalline]], clear and transparent
# relating to the [[ice plant]] ({{taxlink|Mesembyanthemum crystallinum|species|noshow=1}})
# {{label|sh|figuratively}} [[unwelcoming]], [[coldhearted]], [[unfeeling]]
# {{label|sh|figuratively}} {{label|sh|of fear, doubt, or surprise}} [[immobilizing]]

====Declension====
{{sh-adj-full|leden|o|ledenij|e}}

===Usage notes===
Historically, ''{{l|sh|lȅdan}}'' primarily meant “of or relating to ice”, while ''{{l|sh|lȅden}}'' primarily meant “made of ice”, but each was often used for the other; today, ''{{l|sh|lȅden}}'' is by far the more common of the two.

===Synonyms===
* {{l|sh|lȅdan}}

